 

@startuml part3_management_and_escalation_job
actor Admin
actor Staff
participant API
database DB
participant Cron

== 1. Category create/update ==
Admin -> API: POST /categories (name, description, img)
alt name already exists
  API --> Admin: 422 Category name already exists
else valid
  API -> DB: Save new category
  API --> Admin: 201 Created
end

Admin -> API: PATCH /categories/{id}
alt category not found
  API --> Admin: 404 Category not found
else valid
  API -> DB: Update category details
  API --> Admin: 200 OK
end

Admin -> API: DELETE /categories/{id}
alt category referenced by staff/complaint/rule
  API --> Admin: 422 Category in use — deactivate instead
else valid
  API -> DB: Remove category record
  API --> Admin: 200 OK
end

== 2. Staff creation & self-update ==
Admin -> API: POST /staff (name, email, password, categoryId, img)
alt email already exists / invalid categoryId
  API --> Admin: 422 Email exists / invalid categoryId
else valid
  API -> DB: Create user account with staff role
  API -> DB: Create staff profile linked to user and category
  API --> Admin: 201 Created
end

Staff -> API: PATCH /staff/{id} (description, details, img)
alt staff editing another staff profile / admin-only field
  API --> Staff: 403 Access denied
else valid
  API -> DB: Update staff profile details
  API --> Staff: 200 OK
end

== 3. Availability slot creation ==
Admin -> API: POST /staff/availability?staffId= (slots[])
alt slot conflict (same staff, date, startTime) or invalid time range
  API --> Admin: 422 Slot conflict / invalid time range
else staff not found
  API --> Admin: 404 Staff not found
else valid
  API -> DB: Save availability slots as unbooked and active
  API --> Admin: 201 Created
end

== 4. Delete availability slot ==
Admin -> API: DELETE /staff/availability/{slotId}?staffId=
alt slot is booked
  API --> Admin: 422 Slot is booked and cannot be deleted
else valid
  API -> DB: Remove availability slot record
  API --> Admin: 200 OK
end

== 5. Daily escalation check ==
Cron -> API: POST /jobs/escalation-check
loop for each overdue complaint
  API -> DB: Create escalation record for overdue complaint
  API -> DB: Update complaint status to Escalated
  API -> DB: Record progress log entry for Escalated status
  API -> DB: Notify senior admin and resident
end
API --> Cron: 200 OK (escalated count)
@enduml